# The rail on the right edge takes you to the message you point at.
#
# A 120-message thread has one scrollbar and no landmarks: finding the third
# tool run, or the question you asked at the start, means dragging and reading.
# The minimap draws one mark per item — the SAME item list the transcript
# measured and virtualized from — and a click on a mark goes to that item.
#
# A drawn rail is invisible to a text assertion, so what is asserted here is
# the BEHAVIOUR: the thread opens at its end, and each click lands the item
# the mark stands for. The marks are named elements rather than pixels of a
# painted strip, which is also why this clicks by name and not by coordinate.
#
# The fixture repeats question / answer / tool-pile, so mark N*3 is the Nth
# question.
#
# NOTE: expect_no_text takes a BARE single word — see afterhours_gaps.md #47.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_BIG_TRANSCRIPT=1 HANABI_OPEN=rbig

# Opens at the end: the first message is far above the viewport.
require_thread rbig

expect_no_text #0:

click_ui minimap_mark_0
wait_frames 12
expect_text "Follow-up question #0:"

# A mark in the middle goes to the middle, and does not drift back.
click_ui minimap_mark_60
wait_frames 12
expect_text "Follow-up question #20:"
expect_no_text #0:
